Issues Fixed
Chat System Restoration
The chat with agents feature was completely broken due to enhanced inference service failures. The system was attempting to mutate readonly arrays returned from the 0G SDK, causing "Cannot assign to read only property '0'" errors that crashed the service.

Root Cause: The broker.inference.listService() method returns readonly arrays, but the enhanced inference service was directly calling sort() and other mutating operations on them.

Solution: Implemented a copy-first approach that creates mutable copies before any operations:

// Before (failed)
const services = await broker.inference.listService()
services.sort((a, b) => ...) // Error: Cannot assign to read only property

// After (works)  
const rawServices = await broker.inference.listService()
const services = [...rawServices].map(s => ({ ...s })) // Always work with copies
services.sort((a, b) => ...)
Fine-Tuning "Coming Soon" Flag
The fine-tuning disable flag wasn't working because it wasn't accessible on the client side. The flag FT_DISABLED=1 was only available server-side, but the fine-tune page runs on the client.

Solution: Renamed to NEXT_PUBLIC_FT_DISABLED=1 and updated the feature flags system to properly read client-accessible environment variables.

Agent Card UI Visibility
Agent cards were showing "white bars" because text was invisible - using text-gray-600 (dark gray) on a dark gradient background. Users couldn't read agent descriptions or listing information.

Solution: Updated all text colors to use proper contrast:

Changed text-gray-600 to text-white/80 for descriptions
Updated listing info styling from bg-purple-50 text-purple-900 to bg-white/10 border-white/20 text-white
Maintained glassmorphism design consistency
Ledger Auto-Deposit Logic
The system was incorrectly attempting to "top up" accounts that already had sufficient balance, causing "Ledger already exists" errors and unwanted deposit attempts.

Solution: Modified the ensureMinBalance function to not auto-deposit for existing accounts:

if (balance < minBalanceWei) {
  console.log('Balance check complete - not attempting auto-deposit for existing accounts')
  return false // User should explicitly add funds
}
